{"step_index":257,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T13:28:47Z","input_tokens":2509,"cache_read_tokens":87293,"output_tokens":3991,"thinking":"Planning the data generator phase. The prediction engine requires a dataset supporting features like transaction amount deviation, frequency in time windows, account age, device novelty, and IP/location mismatches. These features are critical for model training and evaluation.\n\n\nConsidering adding merchant category and risk history, plus failed attempt indicators, to the feature set. This will improve the dataset's ability to model real-world fraud scenarios. Focusing on the training pipeline, steps to avoid data leakage and properly handle class imbalance are critical.\n\n\nConsidering how to define fraud scenarios and their features. Need to generate realistic fraudulent patterns including high amounts, bursts of transactions, new device usage, suspicious merchant categories (crypto, luxury), IP mismatches, and failed password attempts. The scenarios should explicitly include both legitimate but unusual transactions and coordinated syndicate activity to test the model's ability to discriminate between different risk profiles.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nFraudLens AI - Synthetic Financial Risk Dataset Generator\\nGenerates realistic, chronologically ordered financial transactions with documented fraud typologies:\\n1. Account Takeover (ATO): New device + IP mismatch + failed login attempts.\\n2. Card Testing / Bursts: Rapid succession of micro/medium transactions.\\n3. Sudden Behavioral Deviation: Unusual high amount relative to customer baseline.\\n4. Coordinated Fraud Ring (Syndicate): Multiple accounts sharing identical device & IP.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport json\\nimport random\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\\nimport pandas as pd\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\ndef generate_fraudlens_dataset(n_samples: int = 2500, output_path: str = \\\"data/synthetic_transactions.csv\\\") -> pd.DataFrame:\\n    random.seed(42)\\n    np.random.seed(42)\\n\\n    categories = [\\n        \\\"grocery\\\", \\\"fast_food\\\", \\\"utilities\\\", \\\"entertainment\\\",\\n        \\\"electronics\\\", \\\"travel\\\", \\\"luxury_goods\\\", \\\"crypto_exchange\\\", \\\"gaming\\\"\\n    ]\\n    category_weights = [0.25, 0.20, 0.15, 0.12, 0.10, 0.08, 0.04, 0.03, 0.03]\\n\\n    base_time = datetime(2026, 10, 1, 8, 0, 0)\\n    \\n    # Pool of accounts, devices, IPs, merchants\\n    n_accounts = 250\\n    accounts = [f\\\"ACC-{1000 + i}\\\" for i in range(n_accounts)]\\n    devices = [f\\\"DEV-{2000 + i}\\\" for i in range(180)]\\n    ips = [f\\\"198.51.{i // 256}.{i % 256}\\\" for i in range(1, 150)]\\n    merchants = {cat: [f\\\"MER-{cat[:3].upper()}-{100 + j}\\\" for j in range(10)] for cat in categories}\\n\\n    # Generate customer profiles (historical average amount, primary device, primary IP)\\n    customer_profiles = {}\\n    for acc in accounts:\\n        customer_profiles[acc] = {\\n            \\\"avg_amount\\\": round(float(np.random.lognormal(mean=3.8, sigma=0.6)), 2), # median ~$45\\n            \\\"primary_device\\\": random.choice(devices),\\n            \\\"primary_ip\\\": random.choice(ips),\\n            \\\"account_age_days\\\": random.randint(30, 1200),\\n            \\\"home_country\\\": \\\"US\\\",\\n        }\\n\\n    transactions = []\\n    current_time = base_time\\n\\n    # Gen\n<truncated 7644 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\S Nandhakumar\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\fraudlens-ai\\\\backend\\\\app\\\\ml\\\\data_generator.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
